1
00:00:00,594 --> 00:00:02,344
(Mrs Cooper:)I am not abandoning you.

2
00:00:02,512 --> 00:00:06,182
(Mrs Cooper:)Sheldon, abandoning you is leaving you
in a basket on a church doorstep.

3
00:00:06,641 --> 00:00:10,481
(Mrs Cooper:)I am going to Hollywood
and thank a wax Ronald Reagan...

4
00:00:10,645 --> 00:00:13,685
(Mrs Cooper:)...for his service to our country.

5
00:00:15,108 --> 00:00:17,988
(Sheldon:)We appear to be at a crossroads
in our relationship, Mother.

6
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:21,693
- Well, I guess we are.
- Sorry. Syrup.

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,700
(Sheldon:)All right, Mom. When you're at
the Ripley's Believe It Or Not Museum...

8
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:30,202
(Sheldon:)...if they have an exhibit about a mother
who threw away a chance...

9
00:00:30,373 --> 00:00:34,213
...to spend a day with the world's
most wonderful son, believe it, it's true.

10
00:00:36,797 --> 00:00:39,217
(Leonard:)I hadn't...

11
00:00:41,426 --> 00:00:43,306
(Sheldon:)That lecture was a waste of time.

12
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:46,890
(Sheldon:)I made more accurate diagrams
of the expansion of the early universe...

13
00:00:47,057 --> 00:00:50,307
(Sheldon:)...on the nursery wall
with the contents of my diaper.

14
00:00:52,437 --> 00:00:53,477
(Amy:)Are you getting sick?

15
00:00:53,647 --> 00:00:58,647
(Sheldon:)No, I'm just allergic to people who get
Nobel Prizes for no good reason.

